IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 1, paragraphs 1 to 3B: supplementary provisions relating to contributions of Classes 1, 1A, 1B, 2, 3 and 3A
-- (ssc8, layer 1, first half: aggregation, who pays Class 1, the bar on recovering employer's contributions, the transfer of liability).
-- Source: ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- Paragraph numbers: the rendering drops them. Citations in the Act give 3, 3A and 3B (s 4's "paragraphs 3 to 3B of Schedule 1",
-- src:256) and 8 ("paragraph 8(1)(m) of Schedule 1", src:1881); inside the Schedule, "paragraph 3B above" (src:4708),
-- "paragraph 6 above" (4605, 4683), "paragraph 7" (4587, 4641) and "paragraph 7B" (4686, 4688). Paragraphs 1, 2, 4, 5 and 5A
-- are labelled BY INFERENCE FROM THEIR POSITION: see NOTES.md.
--
-- INPUTS: every "prescribed" circumstance, amount, part or manner, every "regulations so provide", and the Inland Revenue's
-- approval and notices are facts the person (or the lead at the merge) states. Dates the Act gives (19th May 2000) are in the rules;
-- "the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000" is not in this text and is an input.
-- Amounts are in pounds.

§ `Schedule 1 -- paragraphs 1 to 3B`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- Class 1 contributions where earner employed in more than one employment`

-- One payment of earnings in a week, with the person paying it.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` HAS
    `the employer paying it`   IS A STRING
    `the amount in pounds`     IS A NUMBER

-- (1)(a): all earnings paid in that week in respect of one or more employed earner's employments under the same employer are aggregated and
-- treated as a single payment, "except as may be provided by regulations". The list is the earnings paid to the earner in the week.
-- src:4456 | (1) For the purposes of determining whether Class 1 contributions are payable in respect of earnings paid to an earner in a given week and, if so, the amount of the contributions—
-- src:4457 | (a) all earnings paid to him or for his benefit in that week in respect of one or more employed earner’s employments under the same employer shall, except as may be provided by regulations, be aggregated and treated as a single payment of earnings in respect of one such employment; and
-- src:4458 | (b) earnings paid to him or for his benefit in that week by different persons in respect of different employed earner’s employments shall in prescribed circumstances be aggregated and treated as a single payment of earnings in respect of one such employment;
-- src:4459 | and regulations may provide that the provisions of this sub-paragraph shall have effect in cases prescribed by the regulations as if for any reference to a week there were substituted a reference to a period prescribed by the regulations.
@ref sch 1 para 1(1)(a) (src:4456-4459)
GIVEN `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      employer IS A STRING
      payments IS A LIST OF `sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` MEANS
    IF `regulations provide otherwise`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except as may be provided by regulations": the provision of the regulations is an input
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the amount in pounds`)
                        (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the employer paying it` EQUALS employer) payments)))

-- (1)(b): earnings paid in that week by different persons in respect of different employments "shall in prescribed circumstances be
-- aggregated and treated as a single payment".
-- src:4456 | (1) For the purposes of determining whether Class 1 contributions are payable in respect of earnings paid to an earner in a given week and, if so, the amount of the contributions—
-- src:4457 | (a) all earnings paid to him or for his benefit in that week in respect of one or more employed earner’s employments under the same employer shall, except as may be provided by regulations, be aggregated and treated as a single payment of earnings in respect of one such employment; and
-- src:4458 | (b) earnings paid to him or for his benefit in that week by different persons in respect of different employed earner’s employments shall in prescribed circumstances be aggregated and treated as a single payment of earnings in respect of one such employment;
-- src:4459 | and regulations may provide that the provisions of this sub-paragraph shall have effect in cases prescribed by the regulations as if for any reference to a week there were substituted a reference to a period prescribed by the regulations.
@ref sch 1 para 1(1)(b) (src:4456-4459)
GIVEN `the circumstances are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      payments IS A LIST OF `sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 1(1)(b) the single payment of earnings paid by different persons in respect of different employments` MEANS
    IF `the circumstances are prescribed`
    THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `the amount in pounds`) payments))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in prescribed circumstances"; outside them the sub-paragraph says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The parts of a payment or liability apportioned among the employers add up to the whole: the text says "apportioning", and an apportionment divides the whole
-- (reading taken, fork F-S1-1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN whole IS A NUMBER
      parts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1(7) and (8) the parts apportioned add up to the whole` MEANS
    sum parts EQUALS whole

-- (7): a single payment made in respect of two or more employments under different employers is apportioned "to such one or more of the
-- employers as may be prescribed", and "a part apportioned to any employer" is "a separate payment of earnings by him".
-- src:4465 | (7) Where any single payment of earnings is made in respect of two or more employed earner’s employments under different employers, liability for Class 1 contributions shall be determined by apportioning the payment to such one or more of the employers as may be prescribed, and treating a part apportioned to any employer as a separate payment of earnings by him.
@ref sch 1 para 1(7) (src:4465)
GIVEN payment IS A NUMBER
      `the parts apportioned to the employers as prescribed` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`sch 1 para 1(7) the separate payments of earnings by the employers` MEANS
    IF `sch 1 para 1(7) and (8) the parts apportioned add up to the whole` payment `the parts apportioned to the employers as prescribed`
    THEN JUST `the parts apportioned to the employers as prescribed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "apportioning" is not defined; parts that do not add up to the payment are not an apportionment of it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (8): where earnings are aggregated under (1)(b), liability for the secondary contribution is apportioned "in such manner as may be prescribed"
-- between the secondary contributors concerned.
-- src:4466 | (8) Where earnings are aggregated under sub-paragraph (1)(b) above, liability (if any) for the secondary contribution shall be apportioned, in such manner as may be prescribed, between the secondary contributors concerned.
@ref sch 1 para 1(8) (src:4466)
GIVEN `the secondary contribution liability` IS A NUMBER
      `the shares apportioned to the secondary contributors as prescribed` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
`sch 1 para 1(8) the secondary contributors' shares of the liability` MEANS
    IF `sch 1 para 1(7) and (8) the parts apportioned add up to the whole` `the secondary contribution liability` `the shares apportioned to the secondary contributors as prescribed`
    THEN JUST `the shares apportioned to the secondary contributors as prescribed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "apportioned" is not defined; shares that do not add up to the liability are not an apportionment of it
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- method of paying Class 1 contributions`

-- (1): where earnings are paid to an employed earner and liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions, the secondary contributor
-- is, "except in prescribed circumstances", liable in the first instance to pay also the earner's primary contribution, or a prescribed part of it.
-- src:4474 | (1) Where earnings are paid to an employed earner and in respect of that payment liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions, the secondary contributor shall (except in prescribed circumstances), as well as being liable for any secondary contribution of his own, be liable in the first instance to pay also the earner’s primary contribution or a prescribed part of the earner’s primary contribution, on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner; and for the purposes of this Act and the Administration Act contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner shall be taken to be contributions paid by the earner.
@ref sch 1 para 3(1) (src:4474)
GIVEN `earnings are paid to an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions in respect of that payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one of the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earner's primary contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the primary contribution that regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` MEANS
    IF `earnings are paid to an employed earner`
       AND `liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions in respect of that payment`
    THEN
        IF `the case is one of the prescribed circumstances`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except in prescribed circumstances"; what the regulations make of those circumstances is an input
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE
            CONSIDER `the part of the primary contribution that regulations prescribe`
            -- the whole, unless regulations prescribe a part ("the earner's primary contribution or a prescribed part")
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the earner's primary contribution`
            WHEN JUST part THEN JUST part
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where earnings are paid to an employed earner and in respect of that payment liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (1): the secondary contributor pays "on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner", so the earner is not liable in the first instance for what the
-- secondary contributor is liable for.
-- src:4474 | (1) Where earnings are paid to an employed earner and in respect of that payment liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions, the secondary contributor shall (except in prescribed circumstances), as well as being liable for any secondary contribution of his own, be liable in the first instance to pay also the earner’s primary contribution or a prescribed part of the earner’s primary contribution, on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner; and for the purposes of this Act and the Administration Act contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner shall be taken to be contributions paid by the earner.
@ref sch 1 para 3(1) (src:4474)
GIVEN `the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance for the earner's primary contribution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(1) the earner is liable in the first instance for that primary contribution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance for the earner's primary contribution`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the secondary contributor is liable is the previous function's answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner"
    WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST FALSE

-- (1), end: contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner "shall be taken to be contributions paid by the earner".
-- src:4474 | (1) Where earnings are paid to an employed earner and in respect of that payment liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions, the secondary contributor shall (except in prescribed circumstances), as well as being liable for any secondary contribution of his own, be liable in the first instance to pay also the earner’s primary contribution or a prescribed part of the earner’s primary contribution, on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner; and for the purposes of this Act and the Administration Act contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner shall be taken to be contributions paid by the earner.
@ref sch 1 para 3(1) (src:4474)
GIVEN `the contributions are paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(1) the contributions are taken to be paid by the earner` MEANS
    IF `the contributions are paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): the secondary contributor "shall be entitled, subject to and in accordance with regulations, to recover from an earner the amount of any
-- primary Class 1 contribution paid or to be paid by him on behalf of the earner".
-- src:4476 | (3) A secondary contributor shall be entitled, subject to and in accordance with regulations, to recover from an earner the amount of any primary Class 1 contribution paid or to be paid by him on behalf of the earner; and, subject to sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5) below but notwithstanding any other provision in any enactment, regulations under this sub-paragraph shall provide for recovery to be made by deduction from the earner’s earnings, and for it not to be made in any other way.
@ref sch 1 para 3(3) (src:4476)
GIVEN `regulations so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the primary Class 1 contribution paid or to be paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3(3) the amount the secondary contributor is entitled to recover from the earner` MEANS
    IF `regulations so provide`
    THEN JUST `the primary Class 1 contribution paid or to be paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to and in accordance with regulations"; the regulations are an input
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): the regulations "shall provide for recovery to be made by deduction from the earner's earnings, and for it not to be made in any other way",
-- "subject to sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5)".
-- src:4476 | (3) A secondary contributor shall be entitled, subject to and in accordance with regulations, to recover from an earner the amount of any primary Class 1 contribution paid or to be paid by him on behalf of the earner; and, subject to sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5) below but notwithstanding any other provision in any enactment, regulations under this sub-paragraph shall provide for recovery to be made by deduction from the earner’s earnings, and for it not to be made in any other way.
@ref sch 1 para 3(3) (src:4476)
GIVEN `recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one of sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(3) the recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` MEANS
    IF `recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `the case is one of sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5) below": those sub-paragraphs make their own provision
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and for it not to be made in any other way"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (3A), (3B): where an employee receives earnings other than in money from the employer in a tax year, "if and to the extent that regulations so
-- provide" the employer may recover from the employee the primary Class 1 contributions paid on the employee's behalf in respect of those earnings.
-- src:4477 | (3A) Sub-paragraph (3B) applies where a person (“the employee”) who is employed by a particular employer (“the employer”) receives earnings in a form other than money (“non-monetary earnings”) from the employer in a tax year.
-- src:4478 | (3B) If and to the extent that regulations so provide, the employer may recover from the employee, in the prescribed manner, any primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by him on the employee’s behalf in respect of those earnings.
@ref sch 1 para 3(3B) (src:4477-4478)
GIVEN `the employee receives earnings in a form other than money from the employer in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount that regulations allow the employer to recover` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by the employer on the employee's behalf in respect of those earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` MEANS
    IF `the employee receives earnings in a form other than money from the employer in the tax year`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount that regulations allow the employer to recover`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "If and to the extent that regulations so provide"; the regulations are an input
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST allowed THEN
            JUST (min allowed `the primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by the employer on the employee's behalf in respect of those earnings`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sub-paragraph (3B) applies where" the employee receives earnings other than in money from the employer in a tax year
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): sub-paragraph (5) applies where the employee ceases in a tax year ("the cessation year") to be employed by the employer and receives from the
-- employer in the cessation year, after the cessation, or in the next tax year, non-monetary earnings.
-- src:4479 | (4) Sub-paragraph (5) below applies in a case where—
-- src:4480 | (a) a person (“the employee”) ceases in a particular tax year (“the cessation year”) to be employed by a particular employer (“the employer”); and
-- src:4481 | (b) the employee receives from the employer in the cessation year, after the cessation of the employment, or in the next tax year non-monetary earnings.
@ref sch 1 para 3(4) (src:4479-4481)
GIVEN `the employee ceases in the cessation year to be employed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee receives non-monetary earnings from the employer in the cessation year after the cessation of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee receives non-monetary earnings from the employer in the next tax year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3(4) sub-paragraph (5) applies` MEANS
    IF `the employee ceases in the cessation year to be employed by the employer`
       AND (`the employee receives non-monetary earnings from the employer in the cessation year after the cessation of the employment`
            OR `the employee receives non-monetary earnings from the employer in the next tax year`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sub-paragraph (5) below applies in a case where" (a) and (b)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5): if and to the extent that regulations so provide, the employer may recover from the employee, in the prescribed manner, the primary Class 1
-- contributions paid on the employee's behalf in respect of the non-monetary earnings mentioned in (4) (paragraph (b) is shown blank in this text).
-- src:4482 | (5) If and to the extent that regulations so provide, the employer may recover from the employee in such manner as may be prescribed any primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by him on the employee’s behalf in respect of—
-- src:4483 | (a) the non-monetary earnings mentioned in sub-paragraph (4) above; ...
-- src:4484 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref sch 1 para 3(5) (src:4482-4484)
GIVEN `sub-paragraph (5) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount that regulations allow the employer to recover` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by the employer on the employee's behalf in respect of the non-monetary earnings mentioned in sub-paragraph (4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3(5) the amount the employer may recover from the employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sub-paragraph (5) applies`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether sub-paragraph (5) applies is sub-paragraph (4)'s answer, asked as an input
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST applies THEN
        IF applies
        THEN
            CONSIDER `the amount that regulations allow the employer to recover`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "If and to the extent that regulations so provide"; the regulations are an input
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST allowed THEN
                JUST (min allowed `the primary Class 1 contributions paid or to be paid by the employer on the employee's behalf in respect of the non-monetary earnings mentioned in sub-paragraph (4)`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph is for the case sub-paragraph (4) describes
        ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3A -- prohibition on recovery of employer's contributions`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A kind of contribution` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A secondary Class 1 contributions`
    `sch 1 para 3A Class 1A contributions`
    `sch 1 para 3A Class 1B contributions`
    `sch 1 para 3A some other contributions`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A kind of act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person`
    `sch 1 para 3A otherwise recover the contributions from a relevant earner, directly or indirectly`
    `sch 1 para 3A enter into an agreement with any person for such a deduction or for such a recovery`
    `sch 1 para 3A some other act`

-- (1): "a person who is or has been liable to pay any secondary Class 1 or any Class 1A or Class 1B contributions shall not" do (a), (b) or (c);
-- "Subject to sub-paragraph (2)", which the next function answers. TRUE means the person is prohibited from the act.
-- src:4487 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, a person who is or has been liable to pay any secondary Class 1 or any Class 1A or Class 1B contributions shall not—
-- src:4488 | (a) make, from earnings paid by him, any deduction in respect of any such contributions for which he or any other person is or has been liable;
-- src:4489 | (b) otherwise recover any such contributions (directly or indirectly) from any person who is or has been a relevant earner; or
-- src:4490 | (c) enter into any agreement with any person for the making of any such deduction or otherwise for the purpose of so recovering any such contributions.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(1) (src:4487-4490)
GIVEN contributions IS A `sch 1 para 3A kind of contribution`
      act IS A `sch 1 para 3A kind of act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER contributions
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph is about secondary Class 1, Class 1A and Class 1B contributions and says nothing of any other
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A some other contributions` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN contributionsOfTheThreeKinds THEN
        CONSIDER act
        -- the flat negative: "shall not"
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3A make a deduction from earnings paid by the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3A otherwise recover the contributions from a relevant earner, directly or indirectly` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3A enter into an agreement with any person for such a deduction or for such a recovery` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph forbids acts (a) to (c) and says nothing of any other act
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3A some other act` THEN NOTHING

-- (2): sub-paragraph (1) "does not apply to the extent that" an agreement between a secondary contributor and the earner "allows the secondary
-- contributor to recover ... the whole or any part of any secondary Class 1 contribution payable in respect of relevant employment income of that earner".
-- (2A): an agreement is to be disregarded to the extent that it relates to income or contributions of the two kinds named there.
-- (3): sub-paragraph (2) "does not authorise any recovery" in pursuance of an agreement entered into before 19th May 2000, or in respect of a liability
-- arising before the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 (that day is not in this text: an input).
-- src:4491 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) above does not apply to the extent that an agreement between—
-- src:4492 | (a) a secondary contributor, and
-- src:4493 | (b) any person (“the earner”) in relation to whom the secondary contributor is, was or will be such a contributor in respect of the contributions to which the agreement relates,
-- src:4494 | allows the secondary contributor to recover (whether by deduction or otherwise) the whole or any part of any secondary Class 1 contribution payable in respect of relevant employment income of that earner.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(2) (src:4491-4494)
-- src:4495 | (2A) But an agreement in respect of relevant employment income is to be disregarded for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) to the extent that it relates to—
-- src:4496 | (a) relevant employment income which is employment income of the earner by virtue of Chapter 3A of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003 (employment income: securities with artificially depressed market value), or
-- src:4497 | (b) any contribution, or any part of any contribution, liability to which arises as a result of regulations being given retrospective effect by virtue of section 4B(2) (earnings: power to make retrospective provision in consequence of retrospective tax legislation).
@ref sch 1 para 3A(2A) (src:4495-4497)
-- src:4502 | (3) Sub-paragraph (2) above does not authorise any recovery (whether by deduction or otherwise)—
-- src:4503 | (a) in pursuance of any agreement entered into before 19th May 2000; or
-- src:4504 | (b) in respect of any liability to a contribution arising before the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(3) (src:4502-4504)
GIVEN `the amount that the agreement allows the secondary contributor to recover` IS A NUMBER
      `the secondary Class 1 contribution payable in respect of relevant employment income of the earner` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the amount that relates to matters within sub-paragraph (2A)` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the agreement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the day the liability arose` IS A DATE
      `the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement` MEANS
    IF (`the day the agreement was entered into` LESS THAN (Date 19 5 2000))
       OR (`the day the liability arose` LESS THAN `the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sub-paragraph (2) above does not authorise any recovery"
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 ((min `the amount that the agreement allows the secondary contributor to recover`
                     `the secondary Class 1 contribution payable in respect of relevant employment income of the earner`)
                MINUS `the part of the amount that relates to matters within sub-paragraph (2A)`)

-- (2B) and (3A)'s twin in paragraph 3B(1A): the three kinds of amount that are "relevant employment income".
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A(2B) kind of amount` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003`
    `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of ITEPA 2003`
    `sch 1 para 3A(2B) a gain treated as remuneration derived from the earner's employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a)`
    `sch 1 para 3A(2B) some other amount`

-- src:4498 | (2B) For the purposes of sub-paragraphs (2) and (2A) “relevant employment income”, in relation to the earner, means—
-- src:4499 | (a) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003 (restricted securities: charge on certain post-acquisition events),
-- src:4500 | (b) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of that Act (convertible securities: charge on certain post-acquisition events), or
-- src:4501 | (c) a gain that is treated as remuneration derived from the earner’s employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a) above.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(2B) (src:4498-4501)
GIVEN amount IS A `sch 1 para 3A(2B) kind of amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3A(2B) the amount is relevant employment income` MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of ITEPA 2003` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) a gain treated as remuneration derived from the earner's employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a)` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant employment income”, in relation to the earner, means" (a), (b) or (c)
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) some other amount` THEN FALSE

-- (4): "agreement" includes any arrangement or understanding, whether or not legally enforceable.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A(4) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A(4) an agreement`
    `sch 1 para 3A(4) an arrangement`
    `sch 1 para 3A(4) an understanding`
    `sch 1 para 3A(4) something else`

-- src:4505 | (4) In this paragraph—
-- src:4506 | “agreement” includes any arrangement or understanding (whether or not legally enforceable); and
@ref sch 1 para 3A(4) (src:4505-4506)
GIVEN thing IS A `sch 1 para 3A(4) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3A(4) the thing is an agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(4) an agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(4) an arrangement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(4) an understanding` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“agreement” includes any arrangement or understanding"; "includes" does not close the list
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(4) something else` THEN NOTHING

-- (4): "relevant earner", in relation to a person who is or has been liable to pay any contributions, means an earner in respect of whom he is or has been so liable.
-- src:4507 | “relevant earner”, in relation to a person who is or has been liable to pay any contributions, means an earner in respect of whom he is or has been so liable.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(4) (src:4507)
GIVEN `the person is or has been liable to pay the contributions in respect of the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3A(4) the earner is a relevant earner` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant earner” ... means an earner in respect of whom he is or has been so liable"
    `the person is or has been liable to pay the contributions in respect of the earner`

§§ `Paragraph 3B -- transfer of liability to be borne by earner`

-- The facts about one election.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3B an election` HAS
    `it is jointly made by a secondary contributor and the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is for the whole or a part of the secondary contributor's liability to contributions on relevant employment income of the earner to be transferred to the earner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Inland Revenue approved the form of the election by notice before it was made`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Inland Revenue approved the arrangements for securing that the liability transferred will be met by notice before it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was made`                                                                               IS A DATE
    `the day it ceased to have effect in accordance with its terms`                                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day it was revoked jointly by both parties`                                                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day notice terminating it was given to the earner by the secondary contributor`                 IS A MAYBE DATE

-- (1): "This paragraph applies where" (a) and (b).
-- src:4509 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:4510 | (a) an election is jointly made by—
-- src:4511 | (i) a secondary contributor, and
-- src:4512 | (ii) a person (“the earner”) in relation to whom the secondary contributor is or will be such a contributor in respect of contributions on relevant employment income of the earner,
-- src:4513 | for the whole or a part of any liability of the secondary contributor to contributions on any such income to be transferred to the earner; and
-- src:4514 | (b) the election is one in respect of which the Inland Revenue have, before it was made, given by notice to the secondary contributor their approval to both—
-- src:4515 | (i) the form of the election; and
-- src:4516 | (ii) the arrangements made in relation to the proposed election for securing that the liability transferred by the election will be met.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(1) (src:4509-4516)
GIVEN election IS A `sch 1 para 3B an election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(1) this paragraph applies to the election` MEANS
    IF election's `it is jointly made by a secondary contributor and the earner`
       AND election's `it is for the whole or a part of the secondary contributor's liability to contributions on relevant employment income of the earner to be transferred to the earner`
       AND election's `the Inland Revenue approved the form of the election by notice before it was made`
       AND election's `the Inland Revenue approved the arrangements for securing that the liability transferred will be met by notice before it was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where" the election is made jointly and approved
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (1A): "relevant employment income" means the three kinds of amount (the same three as in paragraph 3A(2B)); the kind type is shared.
-- src:4517 | (1A) In this paragraph “relevant employment income”, in relation to the earner, means—
-- src:4518 | (a) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003 (restricted securities: charge on certain post-acquisition events),
-- src:4519 | (b) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of that Act (convertible securities: charge on certain post-acquisition events), or
-- src:4520 | (c) a gain that is treated as remuneration derived from the earner’s employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a) above,
-- src:4521 | and references to contributions on relevant employment income are references to any secondary Class 1 contributions payable in respect of that income.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(1A) (src:4517-4521)
GIVEN amount IS A `sch 1 para 3A(2B) kind of amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(1A) the amount is relevant employment income` MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 426 of ITEPA 2003` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) an amount that counts as employment income of the earner under section 438 of ITEPA 2003` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) a gain treated as remuneration derived from the earner's employment by virtue of section 4(4)(a)` THEN TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant employment income”, in relation to the earner, means" (a), (b) or (c)
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3A(2B) some other amount` THEN FALSE

-- (3): the election "shall continue in force from the time when it is made until whichever of the following first occurs": it ceases to have effect in
-- accordance with its terms; it is revoked jointly by both parties; notice terminating it is given to the earner by the secondary contributor.
-- It is read as no longer in force ON the day of that first event (fork F-S1-3 in NOTES.md). The sub-paragraph is "Subject to sub-paragraphs (7)(b) and (7B)".
GIVEN event IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST eventDay THEN (eventDay LESS THAN day) OR (eventDay EQUALS day)

-- src:4526 | (3) Subject to sub-paragraphs (7)(b) and (7B) below, an election made for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1) above shall continue in force from the time when it is made until whichever of the following first occurs, namely—
-- src:4527 | (a) it ceases to have effect in accordance with its terms;
-- src:4528 | (b) it is revoked jointly by both parties to the election;
-- src:4529 | (c) notice is given to the earner by the secondary contributor terminating the effect of the election.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(3) (src:4526-4529)
GIVEN election IS A `sch 1 para 3B an election`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN election's `the day it was made`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from the time when it is made": before it is made the sub-paragraph says nothing
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE
        IF `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` (election's `the day it ceased to have effect in accordance with its terms`) day
           OR `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` (election's `the day it was revoked jointly by both parties`) day
           OR `sch 1 para 3B(3) the ending event has occurred by the day` (election's `the day notice terminating it was given to the earner by the secondary contributor`) day
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall continue in force ... until whichever of the following first occurs"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): liability which arises while the election is in force and is a liability to pay the contributions on relevant employment income of the earner, or the
-- part of it, to which the election relates "shall be treated ... as a liability falling on the earner, instead of on the secondary contributor".
-- src:4522 | (2) Any liability which—
-- src:4523 | (a) arises while the election is in force, and
-- src:4524 | (b) is a liability to pay the contributions on relevant employment income of the earner, or the part of it, to which the election relates,
-- src:4525 | shall be treated for the purposes of this Act, the Administration Act and Part II of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999 as a liability falling on the earner, instead of on the secondary contributor.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(2) (src:4522-4525)
GIVEN `this paragraph applies to the election` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the election is in force on the day the liability arises` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the liability is to pay the contributions on relevant employment income of the earner, or the part of it, to which the election relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(2) the liability is treated as falling on the earner` MEANS
    IF `this paragraph applies to the election` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the election is in force on the day the liability arises` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the liability is to pay the contributions on relevant employment income of the earner, or the part of it, to which the election relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sub-paragraph says who bears a liability that meets (a) and (b) and says nothing of any other liability
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): an approval may be given either (a) for an election to be made by the secondary contributor and a particular person, or (b) for all elections, or
-- elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3B(4) scope of an approval` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3B(4)(a) for an election by the secondary contributor and a particular person`
    `sch 1 para 3B(4)(b) for all elections, or elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description`

-- src:4530 | (4) An approval given to the secondary contributor for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) above may be given either—
-- src:4531 | (a) for an election to be made by the secondary contributor and a particular person; or
-- src:4532 | (b) for all elections to be made, or to be made in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or by the secondary contributor and persons of a particular description.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(4) (src:4530-4532)
GIVEN scope IS A `sch 1 para 3B(4) scope of an approval`
      `the election is by the secondary contributor and that particular person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election is made in the circumstances for which the approval was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party is one of the particular persons or of the description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(4) the approval covers the election` MEANS
    CONSIDER scope
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(4)(a) for an election by the secondary contributor and a particular person` THEN
        IF `the election is by the secondary contributor and that particular person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an election to be made by the secondary contributor and a particular person"
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(4)(b) for all elections, or elections in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or persons of a particular description` THEN
        IF `the election is made in the circumstances for which the approval was given` AND `the other party is one of the particular persons or of the description`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for all elections to be made, or to be made in particular circumstances, by the secondary contributor and particular persons or ... of a particular description"
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (5): the grounds on which the Inland Revenue "shall be entitled to refuse an approval ... shall include each of" (a) inadequate arrangements, (b) insufficient information.
-- src:4533 | (5) The grounds on which the Inland Revenue shall be entitled to refuse an approval for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) above shall include each of the following—
-- src:4534 | (a) that it appears to the Inland Revenue that adequate arrangements have not been made for securing that the liabilities transferred by the proposed election or elections will be met by the person or persons to whom they would be so transferred; and
-- src:4535 | (b) that it appears to the Inland Revenue that they do not have sufficient information to determine whether or not grounds falling within paragraph (a) above exist.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(5) (src:4533-4535)
GIVEN `it appears to the Inland Revenue that adequate arrangements have not been made for securing that the liabilities transferred will be met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Inland Revenue that they do not have sufficient information to determine whether grounds within paragraph (a) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(5) the Inland Revenue is entitled to refuse the approval` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Inland Revenue that adequate arrangements have not been made for securing that the liabilities transferred will be met`
       OR `it appears to the Inland Revenue that they do not have sufficient information to determine whether grounds within paragraph (a) exist`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "shall include each of the following": the grounds are not limited to (a) and (b)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6): "If, at any time after they have given an approval ..., it appears to the Inland Revenue" (a) the arrangements are proving inadequate or unsatisfactory
-- in any respect, or (b) an election has resulted, or is likely to result, in the avoidance or non-payment of secondary Class 1 contributions, "the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice".
-- src:4536 | (6) If, at any time after they have given an approval for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) above, it appears to the Inland Revenue—
-- src:4537 | (a) that the arrangements that were made or are in force for securing that liabilities transferred by elections to which the approval relates are met are proving inadequate or unsatisfactory in any respect, or
-- src:4538 | (b) that any election to which the approval relates has resulted, or is likely to result, in the avoidance or non-payment of the whole or any part of any secondary Class 1 contributions,
-- src:4539 | the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice to the secondary contributor.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(6) (src:4536-4539)
GIVEN `it appears to the Inland Revenue that the arrangements are proving inadequate or unsatisfactory in any respect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Inland Revenue that an election has resulted, or is likely to result, in the avoidance or non-payment of secondary Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(6) the Inland Revenue may withdraw the approval by notice` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Inland Revenue that the arrangements are proving inadequate or unsatisfactory in any respect`
       OR `it appears to the Inland Revenue that an election has resulted, or is likely to result, in the avoidance or non-payment of secondary Class 1 contributions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, at any time after they have given an approval ..., it appears to the Inland Revenue" (a) or (b) (reading (a): a failed "If" is the text's no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (7A): "the withdrawal date" means (a) the day notice of withdrawal is given, or (b) "such later date as the Inland Revenue may specify in that notice".
-- A later date specified in the notice is the withdrawal date (fork F-S1-4 in NOTES.md); a date not later than the notice day is not "such later date".
-- src:4545 | (7A) In sub-paragraph (7)(b) “the withdrawal date” means—
-- src:4546 | (a) the date on which notice of the withdrawal of the approval is given, or
-- src:4547 | (b) such later date as the Inland Revenue may specify in that notice.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(7A) (src:4545-4547)
GIVEN `the day notice of the withdrawal is given` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice specifies, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1 para 3B(7A) the withdrawal date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice specifies, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day notice of the withdrawal is given`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF `the day notice of the withdrawal is given` LESS THAN specified
        THEN specified
        ELSE `the day notice of the withdrawal is given`

-- (7): the withdrawal "may be either general or confined" to particular elections, and "shall have the effect that the election to which the withdrawal relates
-- has no effect on contributions on relevant employment income if" (i) the income is within (1A)(a) or (b) and the securities, or interest in securities,
-- were acquired after the withdrawal date, or (ii) the income is within (1A)(c) and the right to acquire securities was acquired after that date.
-- src:4540 | (7) The withdrawal by the Inland Revenue of any approval given for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) above—
-- src:4541 | (a) may be either general or confined to a particular election or to particular elections; and
-- src:4542 | (b) shall have the effect that the election to which the withdrawal relates has no effect on contributions on relevant employment income if—
-- src:4543 | (i) that income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(a) or (b) and the securities, or interest in securities, to which it relates were or was acquired after the withdrawal date, or
-- src:4544 | (ii) that income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(c) and the right to acquire securities to which it relates was acquired after that date.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(7) (src:4540-4544)
GIVEN `the withdrawal relates to the election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the securities, or interest in securities, were acquired after the withdrawal date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to acquire securities was acquired after the withdrawal date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(7) the election has no effect on the contributions on the income` MEANS
    IF `the withdrawal relates to the election`
       AND ((`the income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(a) or (b)` AND `the securities, or interest in securities, were acquired after the withdrawal date`)
            OR (`the income is within sub-paragraph (1A)(c)` AND `the right to acquire securities was acquired after the withdrawal date`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall have the effect that the election ... has no effect on contributions on relevant employment income if" (i) or (ii) (reading (a): a failed "if" is the text's no)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (7B): an election "is void ... to the extent that it relates to" (a) relevant employment income that is employment income by virtue of Chapter 3A of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003,
-- or (b) any liability, or part of one, arising as a result of regulations being given retrospective effect by virtue of section 4B(2).
-- src:4548 | (7B) An election is void for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1) to the extent that it relates to —
-- src:4549 | (a) relevant employment income which is employment income of the earner by virtue of Chapter 3A of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003 (employment income: securities with artificially depressed market value), or
-- src:4550 | (b) any liability, or any part of any liability, to a contribution arising as a result of regulations being given retrospective effect by virtue of section 4B(2) (earnings: power to make retrospective provision in consequence of retrospective tax legislation).
@ref sch 1 para 3B(7B) (src:4548-4550)
GIVEN `the part of the transferred liability that relates to income within paragraph (a)` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the transferred liability that relates to liability within paragraph (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3B(7B) the part of the transferred liability for which the election is void` MEANS
    `the part of the transferred liability that relates to income within paragraph (a)` PLUS `the part of the transferred liability that relates to liability within paragraph (b)`

-- (8): where the Inland Revenue have refused or withdrawn their approval, "the person who applied for it or, as the case may be, to whom it was given may appeal".
-- src:4551 | (8) Where the Inland Revenue have refused or withdrawn their approval for the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b) above, the person who applied for it or, as the case may be, to whom it was given may appeal ... against the Inland Revenue’s decision.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(8) (src:4551)
GIVEN `the Inland Revenue have refused the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Inland Revenue have withdrawn the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applied for the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval was given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision` MEANS
    IF (`the Inland Revenue have refused the approval` AND `the person applied for the approval`)
       OR (`the Inland Revenue have withdrawn the approval` AND `the approval was given to the person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person who applied for it or, as the case may be, to whom it was given"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (9): on an appeal notified to the tribunal, the tribunal may (a) dismiss the appeal; (b) remit the decision with a direction; or (c) "in the case of a decision to withdraw
-- an approval", quash it and direct that it is to be treated as never having been made.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3B(9) course` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3B(9)(a) dismiss the appeal`
    `sch 1 para 3B(9)(b) remit the decision with a direction to make such decision as the tribunal thinks fit`
    `sch 1 para 3B(9)(c) quash the decision and direct that it is to be treated as never having been made`
    `sch 1 para 3B(9) some other course`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3B(9) kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to refuse an approval`
    `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval`

-- src:4552 | (9) On an appeal under sub-paragraph (8) above that is notified to the tribunal, the tribunal may—
-- src:4553 | (a) dismiss the appeal;
-- src:4554 | (b) remit the decision appealed against to the Inland Revenue with a direction to make such decision as the tribunal thinks fit; or
-- src:4555 | (c) in the case of a decision to withdraw an approval, quash that decision and direct that that decision is to be treated as never having been made.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(9) (src:4552-4555)
GIVEN `the appeal is notified to the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      decision IS A `sch 1 para 3B(9) kind of decision`
      course IS A `sch 1 para 3B(9) course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(9) the tribunal may take the course` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is notified to the tribunal`
    THEN
        CONSIDER course
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9)(a) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9)(b) remit the decision with a direction to make such decision as the tribunal thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9)(c) quash the decision and direct that it is to be treated as never having been made` THEN
            CONSIDER decision
            WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to withdraw an approval` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a decision to withdraw an approval"
            WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9) a decision to refuse an approval` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sub-paragraph lists three courses and does not say they are the only ones
        WHEN `sch 1 para 3B(9) some other course` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal under sub-paragraph (8) above that is notified to the tribunal"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (10): "Subject to sub-paragraph (12) below, an election under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not apply to any contributions in respect of income which, before the election
-- was made, counted as employment income for a tax year by virtue of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003."
-- src:4556 | (10) Subject to sub-paragraph (12) below, an election under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not apply to any contributions in respect of income which, before the election was made, counted as employment income for a tax year by virtue of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(10) (src:4556)
GIVEN `before the election was made the income counted as employment income for a tax year by virtue of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sub-paragraph (12) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(10) the election applies to the contributions in respect of the income` MEANS
    IF `before the election was made the income counted as employment income for a tax year by virtue of Part 7 of ITEPA 2003`
    THEN
        IF `sub-paragraph (12) applies`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to sub-paragraph (12) below": that sub-paragraph makes its own provision
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an election under sub-paragraph (1) above shall not apply to any contributions in respect of income which, before the election was made, counted as employment income"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sub-paragraph says nothing of income that did not so count
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (12)(a): the day three months on from a day, for "the period of three months beginning with the date of the passing". The period ends the day before that
-- day; where the month three months on is too short for the day (31 January, 30 November), the end is the last day of that month, and the bound returned is the first day of the next.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` MEANS
    IF `sch 1 para 3B(12) the day of the month three months on is in that month` day
    THEN `sch 1 para 3B(12) the same day three months on` day
    ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH (`sch 1 para 3B(12) the same day three months on` day)) (DATE_YEAR (`sch 1 para 3B(12) the same day three months on` day))

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1 para 3B(12) the same day three months on` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH day AT MOST 9
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY day) ((DATE_MONTH day) PLUS 3) (DATE_YEAR day)
    ELSE Date (DATE_DAY day) ((DATE_MONTH day) MINUS 9) ((DATE_YEAR day) PLUS 1)

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(12) the day of the month three months on is in that month` MEANS
    (DATE_MONTH (`sch 1 para 3B(12) the same day three months on` day))
        EQUALS (IF DATE_MONTH day AT MOST 9 THEN (DATE_MONTH day) PLUS 3 ELSE (DATE_MONTH day) MINUS 9)

-- (12): where (a) an election is made before the end of the period of three months beginning with the date of the passing of the 2000 Act and (b) it is expressed to relate to
-- liabilities arising on or after 19th May 2000 and before the making of the election, the liabilities are "deemed to have fallen on the earner (instead of on the secondary
-- contributor); and the secondary contributor shall accordingly be entitled to reimbursement from the earner for any payment made by that contributor in or towards the discharge".
-- src:4561 | (12) Where—
-- src:4562 | (a) an election is made under this paragraph before the end of the period of three months beginning with the date of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000, and
-- src:4563 | (b) that election is expressed to relate to liabilities for contributions arising on or after 19th May 2000 and before the making of the election,
-- src:4564 | this paragraph shall have effect in relation to those liabilities as if sub-paragraph (2) above provided for them to be deemed to have fallen on the earner (instead of on the secondary contributor); and the secondary contributor shall accordingly be entitled to reimbursement from the earner for any payment made by that contributor in or towards the discharge of any of those liabilities.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(12) (src:4561-4564)
GIVEN `the day the election was made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000` IS A DATE
      `the election is expressed to relate to liabilities arising on or after 19th May 2000 and before the making of the election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3B(12) the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` MEANS
    IF (`the day the election was made` LESS THAN (`sch 1 para 3B(12) the day three months on` `the day of the passing of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000`))
       AND `the election is expressed to relate to liabilities arising on or after 19th May 2000 and before the making of the election`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where" (a) the election is made within three months of the passing and (b) it is expressed to relate to the earlier liabilities
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4564 | this paragraph shall have effect in relation to those liabilities as if sub-paragraph (2) above provided for them to be deemed to have fallen on the earner (instead of on the secondary contributor); and the secondary contributor shall accordingly be entitled to reimbursement from the earner for any payment made by that contributor in or towards the discharge of any of those liabilities.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(12) (src:4564)
GIVEN `the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the payment made by the secondary contributor in or towards the discharge of those liabilities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 1 para 3B(12) the reimbursement the secondary contributor is entitled to from the earner` MEANS
    IF `the liabilities are deemed to have fallen on the earner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the payment made by the secondary contributor in or towards the discharge of those liabilities`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is "accordingly", that is, in the case sub-paragraph (12) describes
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (14): "tribunal" means the First-tier Tribunal or, where determined under Tribunal Procedure Rules, the Upper Tribunal.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3B(14) the tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3B(14) the First-tier Tribunal`
    `sch 1 para 3B(14) the Upper Tribunal`

-- src:4566 | (14) In this paragraph “tribunal” means the First-tier Tribunal or, where determined under Tribunal Procedure Rules, the Upper Tribunal.
@ref sch 1 para 3B(14) (src:4566)
GIVEN `the Upper Tribunal is determined under Tribunal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 1 para 3B(14) the tribunal`
`sch 1 para 3B(14) the tribunal is` MEANS
    IF `the Upper Tribunal is determined under Tribunal Procedure Rules`
    THEN `sch 1 para 3B(14) the Upper Tribunal`
    ELSE `sch 1 para 3B(14) the First-tier Tribunal`

§§ `The duties of paragraphs 3(1) and 3A(1) as regulative rules (twins of the decision functions above)`

-- The text gives no deadline for either, so none is written. A DEONTIC result cannot be #ASSERTed on the stable binary (see NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept");
-- the decision functions `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay` and
-- `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` carry the asserted answer, and the #TRACE runs in ssc8-tests-sch1a.l4 show the regulative form.
DECLARE `sch 1 para 3(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3(1) pays the earner's primary contribution on the earner's behalf`

-- src:4474 | (1) Where earnings are paid to an employed earner and in respect of that payment liability arises for primary and secondary Class 1 contributions, the secondary contributor shall (except in prescribed circumstances), as well as being liable for any secondary contribution of his own, be liable in the first instance to pay also the earner’s primary contribution or a prescribed part of the earner’s primary contribution, on behalf of and to the exclusion of the earner; and for the purposes of this Act and the Administration Act contributions paid by the secondary contributor on behalf of the earner shall be taken to be contributions paid by the earner.
@ref sch 1 para 3(1) (src:4474)
`sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor's duty to pay the earner's primary contribution` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor`
    MUST `sch 1 para 3(1) pays the earner's primary contribution on the earner's behalf`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `sch 1 para 3(1) the secondary contributor` BECAUSE "sch 1 para 3(1): the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay the earner's primary contribution"

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions`

DECLARE `sch 1 para 3A(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 3A(1)(a) makes a deduction from earnings paid by the person`
    `sch 1 para 3A(1)(b) otherwise recovers the contributions from a relevant earner`
    `sch 1 para 3A(1)(c) enters into an agreement for such a deduction or recovery`

-- src:4487 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, a person who is or has been liable to pay any secondary Class 1 or any Class 1A or Class 1B contributions shall not—
-- src:4488 | (a) make, from earnings paid by him, any deduction in respect of any such contributions for which he or any other person is or has been liable;
-- src:4489 | (b) otherwise recover any such contributions (directly or indirectly) from any person who is or has been a relevant earner; or
-- src:4490 | (c) enter into any agreement with any person for the making of any such deduction or otherwise for the purpose of so recovering any such contributions.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(1) (src:4487-4490)
`sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on deducting` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions`
    SHANT `sch 1 para 3A(1)(a) makes a deduction from earnings paid by the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions` BECAUSE "sch 1 para 3A(1)(a): shall not make any deduction from earnings paid by the person in respect of such contributions"

-- src:4487 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, a person who is or has been liable to pay any secondary Class 1 or any Class 1A or Class 1B contributions shall not—
-- src:4488 | (a) make, from earnings paid by him, any deduction in respect of any such contributions for which he or any other person is or has been liable;
-- src:4489 | (b) otherwise recover any such contributions (directly or indirectly) from any person who is or has been a relevant earner; or
-- src:4490 | (c) enter into any agreement with any person for the making of any such deduction or otherwise for the purpose of so recovering any such contributions.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(1) (src:4487-4490)
`sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on otherwise recovering` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions`
    SHANT `sch 1 para 3A(1)(b) otherwise recovers the contributions from a relevant earner`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions` BECAUSE "sch 1 para 3A(1)(b): shall not otherwise recover such contributions from a relevant earner"

-- src:4487 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, a person who is or has been liable to pay any secondary Class 1 or any Class 1A or Class 1B contributions shall not—
-- src:4488 | (a) make, from earnings paid by him, any deduction in respect of any such contributions for which he or any other person is or has been liable;
-- src:4489 | (b) otherwise recover any such contributions (directly or indirectly) from any person who is or has been a relevant earner; or
-- src:4490 | (c) enter into any agreement with any person for the making of any such deduction or otherwise for the purpose of so recovering any such contributions.
@ref sch 1 para 3A(1) (src:4487-4490)
`sch 1 para 3A(1) the prohibition on agreeing` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions`
    SHANT `sch 1 para 3A(1)(c) enters into an agreement for such a deduction or recovery`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable to pay the employer's contributions` BECAUSE "sch 1 para 3A(1)(c): shall not enter into an agreement for such a deduction or recovery"
